+3. For interactive problems: simulate the judge with a mock judge script and run the solution against it. Also verify the solution does not crash when the entire input is piped in at once (tokens read via sys.stdin.read().split() where the protocol permits). Prefer token-based input reading when the protocol allows.
+4. Check the solution against the sample inputs/outputs in the statement and on edge cases (minimum sizes, equal values, maximum-size timing where feasible).
+5. If any discrepancy is found, fix it by editing the solution file, then re-run the checks.
+
+Your final message must end with exactly one of these lines:
+REVIEW: ALL PASS
+REVIEW: FAIL <reason>
+"""
+        return self._call_agent(prompt, f"review {round_idx + 1}")
